// How well each lesson matches the task: cosine similarity of the two word sets, each word
// weighted by how rare it is among the lessons (IDF), so "linesdev" counts and "test"
// barely does. The old score (shared words / √lesson words) grew with the prompt's length:
// over 7,654 real person messages (2026-11-07, every chat × its project + global lessons)
// it matched 4 lessons to 83% of them, 26,839 matches, mostly by common words. With this
// score, sampled by band: below 0.2 nearly all are noise ("all done?" → a progress-ping
// lesson), 0.2–0.25 mostly noise ("what extra costs?" → a Rust test lesson), from 0.25 on
// they are on topic ("merge into all-merge" → the wrong-branch deploy lesson). 0.25 with
// at least 2 shared words: 345 matches over 7,406 messages.
export const MATCH_MIN = 0.25;
